# ABP Event Bus

## Event Bus Types
- **Local Event Bus**: In-process messaging (`ILocalEventBus`)
- **Distributed Event Bus**: Inter-process/microservice messaging (`IDistributedEventBus`)

## When to Use Which
- **Microservices**: Use distributed for inter-service, local for internal
- **Modular Monolith**: Use distributed for inter-module (migrates easily to microservices)
- **Simple Monolith**: Use local event bus

## Local Events
```csharp
// Event class
public class ProductCreatedEvent
{
    public Product Product { get; set; }
}

// Handler
public class ProductCreatedEventHandler : ILocalEventHandler<ProductCreatedEvent>, ITransientDependency
{
    public async Task HandleEventAsync(ProductCreatedEvent eventData)
    {
        // Handle event
    }
}

// Publish
await _localEventBus.PublishAsync(new ProductCreatedEvent { Product = product });
```

## Distributed Events (ETO)
```csharp
// Event Transfer Object (in Domain.Shared)
[EventName("MyApp.Product.Created")]
public class ProductCreatedEto
{
    public Guid Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
}

// Handler
public class ProductCreatedEtoHandler : IDistributedEventHandler<ProductCreatedEto>, ITransientDependency
{
    public async Task HandleEventAsync(ProductCreatedEto eventData)
    {
        // Handle distributed event
    }
}
```

## Key Differences
- Local: Can send non-serializable objects (entities)
- Distributed: Must use serializable ETOs, supports outbox/inbox pattern
